# Copy to config.local (git-ignored) and fill in. Environment variables of the same names win.
# Your paid Apple Developer team ID, 10 capital letters and digits. The sure place to find it:
# developer.apple.com > Account > Membership details, "Team ID" (Xcode's Accounts pane may not show
# it, and the code in an "Apple Development" certificate's name is a different identifier: do not use
# it). A free Personal Team cannot sign DriverKit drivers.
RMNET_TEAM_ID=
# A bundle ID you own, for the app; the driver gets <this>.driver. Example: com.example.RMNet
RMNET_BUNDLE_ID=
# 1 builds the driver with IPv6-only preferred on (RMNetIPv6OnlyPreferred in its personalities): a
# DHCP client that asks for RFC 8925's IPv6-Only Preferred option (108) is offered no IPv4 address
# when the modem's IPv4 address is in 192.0.0.0/29 and the link has IPv6, and runs its own 464XLAT
# translator (CLAT) instead. Turn it on only for a network you know provides NAT64, such as an
# IPv6-only network with 464XLAT (T-Mobile US, for one); without NAT64 the client loses IPv4. It is
# off by default because the modem's address does not tell such a network apart: RFC 7335 section 4
# shares 192.0.0.0/29 with DS-Lite, which has no NAT64. 0 or empty leaves it off.
RMNET_IPV6_ONLY_PREFERRED=0
